Forensic Restoration and Architectural Analysis of the "Geek God" CRM Application1. Executive Overview of the Recovery InitiativeThe objective of this comprehensive forensic report is to document the recovery, analysis, and restoration of the "Geek God" Client Relationship Management (CRM) system. This application, built upon the B4X (Basic4Android) framework, serves as a critical interface for financial ledger management, client scheduling, and Google Ecosystem integration. The recovery effort was necessitated by a corruption or versioning control failure in the production codebase, requiring a meticulous reconstruction of logic from a set of fragmented backup artifacts.The analysis draws from four primary source files provided for forensic review: B4XMainPageNewCurrentCode.bas, Copy) m4XMainPage.bas, OldWorkingCode.bas, and B4XMainPage.bak. These artifacts represent different temporal snapshots of the application's lifecycle, ranging from older stable builds to newer, partially broken development versions. By cross-referencing these files, we have successfully identified a significant volume of "lost" subroutines—code blocks that existed in previous working versions but were absent or truncated in the current codebase.This report is structured to strictly follow the recovery protocol: first, identifying the missing routines by name and module provenance; second, defining their interface contracts (declarations); and third, presenting the fully restored code accompanied by deep-dive architectural analysis. The narrative provided herein does not merely list the code but contextualizes it within the broader scope of Android application lifecycle management, OAuth2 security protocols, and responsive user interface design for foldable devices.2. Inventory of Recovered SubroutinesThe first phase of the recovery process involves a strict accounting of the logical units (subroutines) that were salvaged from the backup artifacts. The analysis of the file B4XMainPageNewCurrentCode.bas reveals a functional skeleton but lacks the critical business logic found in Copy) m4XMainPage.bas and the layout stability logic found in OldWorkingCode.bas.The following table provides a consolidated inventory of the missing or compromised subroutines, identifying the primary module (source file) where the most intact version was located. This inventory serves as the master manifest for the restoration effort.Table 1: Master Inventory of Missing and Recovered LogicSubroutine NamePrimary Source ArtifactCategoryRestoration StatusStartLedgerQueueCopy) m4XMainPage.basData ProcessingFully RecoveredProcessNextLedgerCopy) m4XMainPage.basData ProcessingFully RecoveredBatchFetchTabsCopy) m4XMainPage.basAPI IntegrationFully RecoveredBatchGetLedgerCopy) m4XMainPage.basData ParsingFully RecoveredSearchContactCopy) m4XMainPage.basAPI IntegrationFully RecoveredUpdateGoogleContactCopy) m4XMainPage.basAPI IntegrationFully RecoveredAdjustLayoutOldWorkingCode.bas / .bakUI/Layout EnginePartially Recovered (Truncated)LayoutWatchdog_TickOldWorkingCode.basUI/Layout EngineFully RecoveredShowUserSelectionCopy) m4XMainPage.basUser ManagementFully RecoveredCheckSettingsCopy) m4XMainPage.basPersistenceFully Recoveredime_HeightChangedCopy) m4XMainPage.basUI Event HandlingFully RecoveredJobDoneCopy) m4XMainPage.basAsync NetworkingPartially RecoveredOAuth2_AccessTokenAvailableCopy) m4XMainPage.basSecurityFully RecoveredLaunchAppointmentViewCopy) m4XMainPage.basNavigationFully RecoveredbtnCreateLedger_ClickCopy) m4XMainPage.basEvent HandlerFully RecoveredbtnSearch_ClickCopy) m4XMainPage.basEvent HandlerFully RecoveredbtnLogin_ClickCopy) m4XMainPage.basEvent HandlerFully RecoveredGenerateSmartLedgerNone (Reference Only)Data ProcessingMissing / UnrecoverableIt is crucial to note the distinction between "Fully Recovered" and "Partially Recovered." For instance, the AdjustLayout subroutine, critical for the application's responsiveness, is present in the backups but suffers from truncation in the provided text snippets, cutting off the logic that physically resizes the views. Similarly, GenerateSmartLedger is referenced in the event handlers but does not appear in the text body of any provided snippet, suggesting it may reside in a class file not included in this dataset (e.g., a dedicated LedgerManager class).3. Interface Declarations (Signatures)Before analyzing the implementation details, we must establish the interface contracts. These declarations define the input/output boundaries of the recovered components. In the B4X language, strict typing (e.g., As Int, As Map) is enforced, and understanding these signatures is prerequisite to integrating the recovered code back into the main project.3.1. Data Processing and API DeclarationsThe following declarations govern the interaction with Google Drive and Google Sheets. They rely heavily on the HttpJob object from the OkHttpUtils2 library, which handles the asynchronous networking tasks.Public Sub StartLedgerQueue(Name As String)Scope: Public (accessible from other B4XPages).Parameters: Name - The client name used to filter the ledger search.Sub ProcessNextLedgerScope: Private (Internal helper).Parameters: None (Relies on module-level LedgerQueue variable).Sub BatchFetchTabs(Tabs As List, ledgerID As String)Scope: Private (Internal helper).Parameters: Tabs - A list of sheet names; ledgerID - The Google Drive File ID.Sub BatchGetLedger(Job As HttpJob)Scope: Public (Callback target).Parameters: Job - The completed network request object containing the JSON response.3.2. Contact Management DeclarationsThese interfaces manage the connection to the Google People API.Public Sub SearchContact(Query As String)Scope: Public.Parameters: Query - The search string (name, email, or phone).Public Sub UpdateGoogleContact(Params As List)Scope: Public.Parameters: Params - A list containing ``.3.3. UI and Layout Engine DeclarationsThese declarations form the backbone of the adaptive interface, specifically designed to handle dynamic resizing events common on foldable devices like the Samsung Z Fold.Private Sub AdjustLayout(Width As Int, Height As Int)Scope: Private.Parameters: Width / Height - The new dimensions of the container view.Private Sub LayoutWatchdog_TickScope: Private (Timer Event).Parameters: None.Sub ime_HeightChanged(NewHeight As Int, OldHeight As Int)Scope: Public (Event).Parameters: NewHeight / OldHeight - Dimensions representing the visible screen area affected by the software keyboard.3.4. Lifecycle and Security DeclarationsSub CheckSettingsScope: Public.Sub ShowUserSelectionScope: Public.Sub OAuth2_AccessTokenAvailable(Success As Boolean, Token As String)Scope: Public (Callback).Parameters: Success - Boolean flag; Token - The raw OAuth2 access token (if successful).Public Sub CheckOAuth(Intent As Intent)Scope: Public.Parameters: Intent - The Android system intent carrying the deep-link redirect uri.4. Forensic Restoration: The Recovered Source CodeThis section presents the recovered source code in its entirety, organized by functional domain. Each block is accompanied by an extensive analysis of its logic, dependencies, and architectural significance.4.1. The "Smart Ledger" EngineThe core value proposition of the Geek God application appears to be its ability to aggregate financial data from distributed Google Sheets ("Ledgers"). The recovery of the following subroutines restores the application's ability to search, fetch, and compute client spend data.4.1.1. Subroutine: StartLedgerQueueSource Artifact: Copy) m4XMainPage.bas This subroutine acts as the entry point for the financial analysis workflow. When a user queries a client, this routine is triggered to find the relevant spreadsheet on Google Drive.VB.NetPublic Sub StartLedgerQueue(Name As String)
    ' Initialize the processing queues and temporary storage
    LedgerQueue.Initialize
    IssuesHistory.Initialize
    
    ' Reset the temporary profile metrics
    TempProfile.Put("RawTotalSpend", 0.0)
    TempProfile.Put("RawVisitCount", 0)
    TempProfile.Put("LastVisit", "New Client")
    
    ' Initialize the network request
    Dim job As HttpJob
    job.Initialize("SearchLedgerFiles", Me)
    
    ' Construct the Google Drive API Query
    ' Logic: Find files with "Geek God Ledger" in the name that are NOT in the trash
    Dim q As String = "name contains 'Geek God Ledger' and trashed = false"
    Dim su As StringUtils
    
    ' Execute the API call
    job.Download("https://www.googleapis.com/drive/v3/files?q=" & su.EncodeUrl(q, "UTF8"))
    job.GetRequest.SetHeader("Authorization", "Bearer " & OAuth2.access_token)
End Sub
Architectural Analysis:The logic here implies a "convention over configuration" architecture. The application does not store the Ledger ID in a database; instead, it dynamically searches for it every time using the string literal "Geek God Ledger". This design choice eliminates the need for a local database synchronization but creates a fragility: if the spreadsheet is renamed on Google Drive, the application will fail to find the data.The use of TempProfile suggests that the application uses a Map object as a data transfer object (DTO) to hold client state during the asynchronous fetching process. The explicit initialization of RawTotalSpend to 0.0 ensures that the accumulation logic in later subroutines works correctly without type casting errors.4.1.2. Subroutine: ProcessNextLedgerSource Artifact: Copy) m4XMainPage.bas This subroutine implements a recursive queue pattern. Since a search might return multiple ledger files (e.g., one for 2024, one for 2025), this routine iterates through them one by one.VB.NetSub ProcessNextLedger
    ' Base Case: If the queue is empty, we are done.
    If LedgerQueue.Size = 0 Then
        ' Finalize the data formatting
        Dim total As Double = TempProfile.Get("RawTotalSpend")
        TempProfile.Put("TotalSpend", NumberFormat2(total, 1, 2, 2, True))
        TempProfile.Put("VisitCount", TempProfile.Get("RawVisitCount"))
        TempProfile.Put("IssuesList", IssuesHistory)
        
        ' Pass the completed profile to the UI layer
        CallSub2(SearchScreen, "ShowProfile", TempProfile)
        Return
    End If
    
    ' Recursive Step: Get the next ID and remove it from the queue
    CurrentLedgerID = LedgerQueue.Get(0)
    LedgerQueue.RemoveAt(0)
    
    ' Fetch Metadata for this specific spreadsheet
    Dim job As HttpJob
    job.Initialize("GetSheetMetadata", Me)
    job.Tag = CurrentLedgerID
    job.Download("https://sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/" & CurrentLedgerID)
    job.GetRequest.SetHeader("Authorization", "Bearer " & OAuth2.access_token)
End Sub
Architectural Analysis:This routine bridges the gap between the "Search" phase and the "Fetch" phase. The critical insight here is the use of CallSub2. This indicates that the MainPage acts as a controller, and once the data processing is complete, it delegates the display logic to SearchScreen. This separation of concerns (Logic vs. UI) is a hallmark of the B4XPages architecture.The formatting logic (NumberFormat2) ensures that the raw double value (e.g., 150.5) is converted to a currency-friendly string (e.g., "150.50") before reaching the UI, ensuring display consistency.4.1.3. Subroutine: BatchFetchTabsSource Artifact: Copy) m4XMainPage.bas To avoid the performance penalty of fetching each sheet tab individually (which would result in dozens of HTTP round-trips), this subroutine constructs a "Batch Get" request.VB.NetSub BatchFetchTabs(Tabs As List, ledgerID As String)
    Dim sb As StringBuilder
    sb.Initialize
    Dim su As StringUtils
    
    ' Iterate through all identified tabs to build the range query
    For Each tabName As String In Tabs
        Dim range As String = tabName & "!A:G"
        sb.Append("&ranges=").Append(su.EncodeUrl(range, "UTF8"))
    Next
    
    ' Execute the Batch Request
    Dim job As HttpJob
    job.Initialize("BatchGetLedger", Me)
    job.Download("https://sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/" & ledgerID & "/values:batchGet?majorDimension=ROWS" & sb.ToString)
    job.GetRequest.SetHeader("Authorization", "Bearer " & OAuth2.access_token)
End Sub
Architectural Analysis:The application specifically requests columns A:G (!A:G). This optimization reduces payload size by ignoring columns H and beyond, which presumably contain irrelevant data. The use of StringBuilder is a performance optimization for string concatenation in loop structures, vital for Android memory management when dealing with large numbers of tabs.4.1.4. Subroutine: BatchGetLedgerSource Artifact: Copy) m4XMainPage.bas This is the most complex data parsing routine recovered. It handles the raw JSON response from Google Sheets, extracts rows matching the client's name, and aggregates the financial totals.VB.NetSub BatchGetLedger(Job As HttpJob)
    Dim parser As JSONParser
    parser.Initialize(Job.GetString)
    Dim rootMap As Map = parser.NextObject
    Dim valueRanges As List = rootMap.Get("valueRanges")
    
    ' Retrieve current accumulation state
    Dim currentSpend As Double = TempProfile.Get("RawTotalSpend")
    Dim currentVisits As Int = TempProfile.Get("RawVisitCount")
    Dim lastDateStr As String = TempProfile.Get("LastVisit")
    Dim targetName As String = TempProfile.Get("Name").As(String).ToLowerCase
    
    ' Iterate through every sheet (range) returned
    For Each rangeObj As Map In valueRanges
        If rangeObj.ContainsKey("values") Then
            Dim rows As List = rangeObj.Get("values")
            For Each row As List In rows
                If row.Size > 1 Then
                    Dim rowName As String = row.Get(1) ' Column B: Client Name
                    
                    ' Fuzzy Match: Check if the row contains the target name
                    If rowName.ToLowerCase.Contains(targetName) Then
                        currentVisits = currentVisits + 1
                        Dim dStr As String = row.Get(0) ' Column A: Date
                        Dim issue As String = "General"
                        Dim resolved As String = "N/A"
                        Dim payment As String = "$0.00"
                        
                        ' Safe extraction of optional columns
                        If row.Size > 4 Then issue = row.Get(4)      ' Column E
                        If row.Size > 5 Then resolved = row.Get(5)   ' Column F
                        If row.Size > 6 Then                         ' Column G
                            payment = row.Get(6)
                            ' Data Cleaning: Remove currency symbols for math
                            Dim cleanPay As String = payment.Replace("$", "").Replace(",", "").Trim
                            If IsNumber(cleanPay) Then currentSpend = currentSpend + cleanPay
                        End If
                        
                        lastDateStr = dStr
                        
                        ' Build the History Log Item
                        Dim historyItem As String = dStr & " - " & issue & " - " & resolved & " - " & payment
                        IssuesHistory.InsertAt(0, historyItem)
                    End If
                End If
            Next
        End If
    Next
    
    ' Update the accumulation state
    TempProfile.Put("RawTotalSpend", currentSpend)
    TempProfile.Put("RawVisitCount", currentVisits)
    TempProfile.Put("LastVisit", lastDateStr)
    
    ' Trigger the next file in the queue
    ProcessNextLedger
End Sub
Architectural Analysis:The parsing logic reveals the structure of the underlying Google Sheet:Column A (Index 0): Date of visit.Column B (Index 1): Client Name (used for matching).Column E (Index 4): The "Issue" reported.Column F (Index 5): Resolution status.Column G (Index 6): Payment amount.The code includes defensive programming, specifically If row.Size > 4 and If IsNumber(cleanPay). This is critical when dealing with user-generated spreadsheets where columns might be empty or contain text in numeric fields. The logic uses a Contains match (rowName.ToLowerCase.Contains(targetName)), which acts as a rudimentary fuzzy search. This means a search for "Mike" would match "Mike Smith" and "Big Mike," potentially aggregating data from multiple distinct clients if names are not unique.4.2. Contact and CRM LogicThe application extends beyond passive ledger reading to active contact management via the Google People API.4.2.1. Subroutine: SearchContactSource Artifact: Copy) m4XMainPage.bas VB.NetPublic Sub SearchContact(Query As String)
    Log("Step 1: Searching Contacts for " & Query)
    If OAuth2.access_token = "" Then
        OAuth2.GetAccessToken
        Return
    End If
    
    CurrentSearchQuery = Query.ToLowerCase.Trim

    Dim job As HttpJob
    job.Initialize("SearchContact", Me)
    ' Request a massive payload of fields
    job.Download("https://people.googleapis.com/v1/people/me/connections?personFields=names,phoneNumbers,addresses,biographies,memberships&pageSize=1000")
    job.GetRequest.SetHeader("Authorization", "Bearer " & OAuth2.access_token)
End Sub
Architectural Analysis:This routine requests pageSize=1000, attempting to fetch the user's entire address book in a single request. While simple, this is a scalability risk. If the user has 1,001 contacts, the API will paginate, and this code (as written) does not handle the nextPageToken. Consequently, clients beyond the first 1000 would be invisible to the app.4.2.2. Subroutine: UpdateGoogleContactSource Artifact: Copy) m4XMainPage.bas This complex routine constructs a JSON PATCH request to modify a contact on the server.VB.NetPublic Sub UpdateGoogleContact(Params As List)
    Dim ResourceName As String = Params.Get(0)
    Dim Etag As String = Params.Get(1)
    Dim NewNotes As String = Params.Get(2)
    Dim NewLabel As String = Params.Get(3)
    
    ' Map friendly labels to internal Group IDs
    Dim targetGroupID As String = ""
    Select NewLabel
        Case "Blacklisted"
            targetGroupID = Starter.GroupID_Blacklisted
        Case "Preferred"
            targetGroupID = Starter.GroupID_Preferred
        Case Else
            targetGroupID = Starter.GroupID_Client
    End Select
    
    ' Build the JSON Payload
    Dim personMap As Map
    personMap.Initialize
    personMap.Put("etag", Etag)
    personMap.Put("biographies", Array(CreateMap("value": NewNotes, "contentType": "TEXT_PLAIN")))
    
    Dim fields As String = "biographies"
    
    ' Only add membership update if a group is defined
    If targetGroupID <> "" Then
        personMap.Put("memberships", Array(CreateMap("contactGroupMembership": CreateMap("contactGroupResourceName": targetGroupID))))
        fields = fields & ",memberships"
    End If
    
    Dim json As JSONGenerator
    json.Initialize(personMap)
    
    Dim job As HttpJob
    job.Initialize("UpdateContact", Me)
    ' PATCH request with specific updatePersonFields
    job.PatchString("https://people.googleapis.com/v1/" & ResourceName & ":updateContact?updatePersonFields=" & fields, json.ToString)
    job.GetRequest.SetContentType("application/json")
    job.GetRequest.SetHeader("Authorization", "Bearer " & OAuth2.access_token)
End Sub
Architectural Analysis:This logic handles the categorization of clients into "Blacklisted," "Preferred," or standard "Client" groups. It relies on global variables stored in the Starter service (Starter.GroupID_...). This implies that during the app's initialization (likely in CheckContactGroups which is referenced but missing), the app fetches and caches these Group IDs. The use of Etag is a critical concurrency control; if the contact was modified on another device (e.g., the web interface) since the app last fetched it, the API will reject this patch to prevent overwriting data.4.3. Adaptive UI and Layout Logic (The Foldable Engine)One of the most distinct features of this application is its explicit support for the Samsung Z Fold form factor. The recovered code shows a sophisticated, if manual, approach to responsive design.4.3.1. Subroutine: LayoutWatchdog_TickSource Artifact: OldWorkingCode.bas This subroutine is the "heartbeat" of the responsive layout system.VB.NetPrivate Sub LayoutWatchdog_Tick
    ' Guard Clause: Ensure the root view exists
    If Root.IsInitialized = False Then Return
    
    ' Get current physical dimensions
    Dim RealWidth As Int = GetDeviceLayoutValues.Width
    Dim RealHeight As Int = GetDeviceLayoutValues.Height
    
    ' Threshold Check: Only trigger if width changes by > 20 units
    If Abs(RealWidth - LastAppliedWidth) > 20 Then
        ' Force the layout to update with animation
        Root.SetLayoutAnimated(0, 0, 0, RealWidth, RealHeight)
        
        ' Trigger the internal adjustment logic
        AdjustLayout(RealWidth, RealHeight)
    End If
End Sub
Architectural Analysis:Standard Android activities recreate themselves upon rotation or screen size change. However, B4XPages typically handle configuration changes internally to maintain state. On foldable devices, the screen width can change dynamically when the device is unfolded. This watchdog timer (running likely every 200-500ms) polls the dimensions. The > 20 threshold acts as a hysteresis filter to prevent jittering or infinite loops if the reported width fluctuates slightly by a pixel or two.4.3.2. Subroutine: AdjustLayout (Truncated)Source Artifacts: OldWorkingCode.bas , B4XMainPage.bak This is the most critical UI routine, yet it is partially truncated in all available backups. However, the recovered portion establishes the initialization safeguards.VB.NetPrivate Sub AdjustLayout(Width As Int, Height As Int)
    Log("--- AdjustLayout Called --- Width: " & Width & " | Height: " & Height)

