    Log("List Parent Check: IsInitialized=" & lv.Parent.IsInitialized & " | Parent is Root? " & (lv.Parent = Root))
    
    '......
End Sub
Gap Analysis & Reconstruction Theory:The code cuts off right after logging the state of the lstTodayApts (List View). Based on the calculation of HeaderBottom, the missing code almost certainly sets the Top, Left, Width, and Height properties of the pnlStats (Statistics Panel) and lstTodayApts to fit the remaining screen real estate. The presence of the AdjustLayout call inside LayoutWatchdog confirms that this routine is responsible for the physical repositioning of elements when the device folds or unfolds.4.3.3. Subroutine: ime_HeightChangedSource Artifact: Copy) m4XMainPage.bas This handles the onscreen keyboard (IME) interactions.VB.NetSub ime_HeightChanged (NewHeight As Int, OldHeight As Int)
    ' This moves the popup card in the SearchPage when the keyboard opens
    CallSub3(SearchScreen, "AdjustForKeyboard", NewHeight, Root.Height)
End Sub
Architectural Analysis:This is a classic mobile development problem: the keyboard covers the input field. The MainPage captures this global event but delegates the actual UI movement to the SearchScreen via CallSub3. This confirms that the SearchScreen is a child of the MainPage but maintains its own layout logic.4.4. Security and Identity LogicThe application employs a robust, if manually implemented, identity and security layer.4.4.1. Subroutine: OAuth2_AccessTokenAvailableSource Artifact: Copy) m4XMainPage.bas VB.NetSub OAuth2_AccessTokenAvailable(Success As Boolean, Token As String)
    Log("Event: AccessTokenAvailable. Success=" & Success)
    If Success Then
