End Sub
Architectural Analysis:This routine, coupled with DetectUserIdentity (from B4XMainPageNewCurrentCode.bas), enforces a strict two-user policy. The system is hardcoded for "Mike" (using a ZFold) and "Erin" (using an S23). This tight coupling between hardware and user identity is unusual for commercial software but typical for bespoke internal tools. The use of Wait For creates a non-blocking pause, allowing the rest of the UI thread to remain responsive while the user makes a selection.4.5. The "JobDone" Network HandlerSource Artifact: Copy) m4XMainPage.bas The JobDone subroutine is the universal receiver for all API calls initiated by HttpJob. While the provided snippet is truncated, its structure is standard for B4X applications.VB.NetSub JobDone(Job As HttpJob)
