Restoration Note:Although the body is missing, we can infer the contents based on the Job.Initialize calls found in other subroutines. The Select Case structure must handle:"SearchLedgerFiles" -> Parses the JSON list of files and populates LedgerQueue."GetSheetMetadata" -> Parses the sheet names and calls BatchFetchTabs."BatchGetLedger" -> Calls BatchGetLedger(Job)."SearchContact" -> Parses the People API response."UpdateContact" -> Confirms the edit was successful.5. Gap Analysis and Remaining RisksDespite the successful recovery of approximately 95% of the logic, specific gaps remain that require developer attention during the recompilation phase.5.1. The "GenerateSmartLedger" VoidThe event handler btnCreateLedger_Click  explicitly calls GenerateSmartLedger. However, this subroutine is not present in any of the four provided backup files.Hypothesis: This logic likely resides in a separate class module (perhaps CloseOut or a utility class) that was not included in the dump.Impact: Without this routine, the "Create Ledger" button will crash the application.5.2. Truncated Layout LogicThe AdjustLayout subroutine is missing its functional body.Impact: The application will launch, but the UI elements (Statistics Panel, Appointment List) will likely be piled on top of each other at coordinates (0,0) or remain in their design-time positions, failing to adapt to the screen size.Remediation: The logic needs to be rewritten using the HeaderBottom variable to vertically stack the pnlStats and lstTodayApts.5.3. Missing Group ID InitializationThe UpdateGoogleContact routine relies on Starter.GroupID_Blacklisted, etc. The code to fetch these IDs from the Google API (referenced as CheckContactGroups) is missing.Impact: Attempting to update a contact's group will fail or default to an empty string, causing API errors.6. ConclusionThe forensic analysis of the "Geek God" CRM codebase reveals a sophisticated, custom-built application tailored for a specific operational workflow involving two distinct user personas and hardware profiles. The application leverages advanced B4X features including ResumableSubs (Wait For), HttpJob for RESTful integration, and B4XPages for state management.By combining the logic from Copy) m4XMainPage.bas (which contained the deep API logic) and OldWorkingCode.bas (which contained the critical layout stability timers), we have synthesized a restoration plan that recovers the vast majority of the lost functionality. The remaining gaps are identifiable and can be reconstructed using the architectural patterns established in the recovered code.This report serves as the blueprint for the immediate reassembly of the application. The recommended next step is to paste the "Recovered Source Code" sections into a fresh B4XMainPage.bas file, keeping the Initialize and B4XPage_Created from the "NewCurrentCode" file as the base structure.



